      "updated_at": "2026-07-30T14:51:30Z",
      "author_association": "MEMBER",
      "body": "According to one of the mail list moderators, you should have received the following message:\r\n\r\n\"Upon cursory inspection, this submission appears to have a significant amount of LLM generated text combined with the request for human review, with few signs of prior inquiry whether this particular approach was even of interest to the community. This has been a recurring problematic pattern in submission to the list. Review has always been the bottleneck, not the generation of ideas. Working out all the details prior to establishing whether there is interest is counter-productive. LLMs exacerbate the issue. We understand this may be disappointing, and can certainly imagine this may all be well-intentioned, but we hope you can also see our end as well. Of course you are always free to publish and seek review elsewhere. Thank you for your time.\"\r\n\r\nPerhaps submit a short, high quality, well considered, human written presentation of your idea to the mail list?",
